# Implementation Plan: Universal Business-Feature Module Architecture Across All Frameworks

This plan details the comprehensive restructuring of **all 5 supported frameworks** (**Django, Flutter Mobile, Flutter Desktop, Vue.js, and React.js**) to enforce a strict **self-contained business-feature module-based architecture**.

---

## Core Rule & Golden Principle

> **All business-feature-related code MUST remain inside that feature's module.**  
> A feature module MUST own 100% of its resources (pages/screens, components/widgets, services, state management, models/types, routes, API integrations, tasks, tests, and feature-specific utilities).

If a feature module (e.g. `customers`) is removed, **all** related pages, components, services, state, routes, types, tasks, and tests are deleted with it, leaving zero orphaned business code in global directories.

Global directories (`core/`, `shared/`, `common/`) are strictly reserved for **truly shared non-domain application infrastructure**.

---

## Target Framework Architecture Specifications

### 1. Django Architecture
- **Core Infrastructure (`project/core/`)**: Authentication mechanisms, custom permissions, exception handling, base serializers/models, common utilities.
- **Business Modules (`project/modules/<feature_name>/`)**:
  - `models/` (or `models.py`)
  - `views/` (or `views.py`)
  - `serializers/` (or `serializers.py`)
  - `services/` (or `services.py`)
  - `urls/` (or `urls.py`)
  - `tasks/` (or `tasks.py`)
  - `tests/` (or `tests.py`)
  - Example modules: `modules/users/`, `modules/customers/`, `modules/reports/`.

```text
django/
└── foundation/
    ├── core/
    │   ├── authentication/
    │   ├── permissions/
    │   ├── exceptions/
    │   └── common/
    ├── modules/
    │   ├── users/
    │   ├── customers/
    │   └── reports/
    └── settings/
```

---

### 2. Flutter Mobile Architecture
- **Core Infrastructure (`lib/core/`)**: SQLite/Drift database connection, network client & interceptors, authentication state, common adaptive widgets.
- **Feature Modules (`lib/features/<feature_name>/`)**:
  - `presentation/` (pages/screens, widgets, providers/viewmodels)
  - `domain/` (entities, use cases)
  - `data/` (repositories, data sources, DTOs)
  - Example features: `features/authentication/`, `features/customers/`, `features/reports/`.

```text
flutter/mobile/
└── foundation/
    └── lib/
        ├── core/
        │   ├── database/
        │   ├── network/
        │   ├── authentication/
        │   └── common/
        └── features/
            ├── customers/
            │   ├── data/
            │   ├── domain/
            │   └── presentation/
            └── reports/
```

---

### 3. Flutter Desktop Architecture
- **Core Infrastructure (`lib/core/`)**: Hardware integration (serial port communication, RS232 stream buffers), Drift encrypted database setup, Windows/Linux native bridge wrappers, window controls, common UI components.
- **Feature Modules (`lib/features/<feature_name>/`)**:
  - `presentation/` (desktop views/pages, widgets, providers)
  - `domain/` (desktop models, use cases)
  - `data/` (hardware repositories, DAOs)
  - Example features: `features/weighing/`, `features/customers/`, `features/reports/`.

```text
flutter/desktop/
└── foundation/
    └── lib/
        ├── core/
        │   ├── hardware/          # Serial communication & hardware drivers
        │   ├── db/                # Drift SQLite WAL mode DB
        │   └── common/            # Shared desktop widgets
        └── features/
            ├── weighing/
            └── customers/
```

---

### 4. Vue.js Architecture
- **Shared Infrastructure (`src/shared/`)**: UI primitives (Button.vue, Modal.vue, Dialog.vue), shared generic composables (useTheme, useWindowSize), Axios API Client factory, shared types.
- **Feature Modules (`src/modules/<feature_name>/`)**:
  - `pages/` (CustomerList.vue, CustomerDetails.vue, CustomerCreate.vue)
  - `components/` (CustomerTable.vue, CustomerForm.vue)
  - `services/` (customerApi.ts)
  - `stores/` (customerStore.ts)
  - `composables/` (useCustomers.ts)
  - `types/` (customer.ts)
  - `routes/` (customerRoutes.ts)
  - `tests/` (CustomerTable.spec.ts)
  - `index.ts`

```text
vuejs/
└── foundation/
    └── src/
        ├── shared/
        │   ├── components/
        │   ├── composables/
        │   ├── services/
        │   └── types/
        └── modules/
            └── customers/
```

---

### 5. React.js Architecture
- **Shared Infrastructure (`src/shared/`)**: UI primitives (Button.tsx, Modal.tsx, ErrorBoundary.tsx), generic custom hooks (useDebounce, useTheme), base HTTP client, pure utils, core types.
- **Feature Modules (`src/modules/<feature_name>/`)**:
  - `pages/` (CustomerList.tsx, CustomerDetails.tsx, CustomerCreate.tsx)
  - `components/` (CustomerTable.tsx, CustomerForm.tsx)
  - `services/` (customerApi.ts)
  - `store/` (customerSlice.ts)
  - `hooks/` (useCustomers.ts)
  - `types/` (customer.ts)
  - `routes/` (customerRoutes.ts)
  - `tests/` (CustomerTable.test.tsx)
  - `index.ts`

```text
react/
└── foundation/
    └── src/
        ├── shared/
        │   ├── components/
        │   ├── hooks/
        │   ├── services/
        │   └── types/
        └── modules/
            └── customers/
```

